Implemented the presenter-layer transaction in the Apple crate. Each frame now prepares a configured `CALayer` off-hierarchy, then uses one guarded `addSublayer` or `replaceSublayer_with` call. `WindowRecord` takes ownership only after that call succeeds; `Window` remains weak. The prior visible layer is not mutated, and directly supplied contents are not invalidated with `setNeedsDisplay`.

The pure failure-path test confirms that a failed publish callback leaves prior presenter state intact. It does **not** prove AppKit runtime behavior.

All requested checks passed: package check, package tests (**48 passed**), and WO validator. The full named Cargo test output and individual results are in [test.log](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.cache/WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01/worker/artifacts/WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01/test.log). Hashes and exact outcomes are recorded in [verification.json](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.cache/WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01/worker/artifacts/WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01/verification.json).

